Tintinnabulum — third-party material and attribution
====================================================

Tintinnabulum is an independent project, not a fork. Its engine (event
contract, adaptive mapper, voice allocator, Canvas renderer, ingest server)
was written for this repository. Two things nonetheless come from elsewhere
and are acknowledged here.


1. Audio samples — sounds/
--------------------------

The 108 files under sounds/ (celesta/, clav/, swells/) are redistributed from:

    Listen to Wikipedia
    https://github.com/hatnote/listen-to-wikipedia
    Copyright (c) 2013, Stephen LaPorte and Mahmoud Hashemi
    BSD 3-Clause License

The full text of that license is reproduced below, as its terms require.

Provenance note: that project's README states the sounds were processed with
SoX and that the project was inspired by BitListen by Maximillian Laumeister.
The origin of the raw samples is not documented upstream, so their provenance
prior to 2013 could not be established. Anyone with a stricter provenance
requirement should use the built-in synthesis kit instead, which needs no
audio files at all:

    new Sonifier({ kit: 'synth' })


2. Sonification concept
-----------------------

The core idea — a bell for growth, a plucked string for shrinkage, pitch
inversely proportional to the size of the change — originates with Listen to
Wikipedia, and through it with BitListen. Tintinnabulum generalises that idea
to arbitrary data; it does not claim to have invented it.


